argus-scanner for Debian
========================

Architecture-independent package
--------------------------------
The binary package is "Architecture: all".  It contains only the pure-Python
wheel of argus, the launchers and the man pages: no compiled objects and no
third-party binaries.  The same .deb therefore works on every architecture
that Python supports, and Debian Policy 4.13 is satisfied.

Private Python runtime
----------------------
During configuration the package creates

  /var/lib/argus-scanner/runtime

a virtual environment with argus and its dependencies (tree-sitter,
tree-sitter-java, Semgrep and its closure) downloaded from the Python package
index.  This is why python3-tree-sitter, python3-tree-sitter-java and Semgrep
do not have to exist in the archive, and why nothing has to be vendored.

Consequences:

  * installation needs network access, or a wheel directory (see below);
  * about 380 MB are used under /var/lib;
  * Python 3.10 or newer is required, because current Semgrep releases do not
    support older interpreters.

If the download is impossible the installation still succeeds.  The
launchers then print what to do, and the runtime can be provisioned later.

Provisioning, updating and removing the runtime
-----------------------------------------------
  sudo argus-setup-runtime                  # install or rebuild, latest deps
  sudo argus-setup-runtime --list           # versions and size
  sudo argus-setup-runtime --upgrade-semgrep
                                            # update only Semgrep
  sudo argus-setup-runtime --semgrep 1.90.0 # pin Semgrep
  sudo argus-setup-runtime --remove         # delete the runtime
  sudo argus-setup-runtime --wheelhouse DIR # install offline from wheels

A freshly installed Semgrep is verified by running it; if it does not start,
the previous version is reinstalled automatically.

Offline installation
--------------------
On a machine with network access, prepare wheels for the target platform
(the same Python version and architecture as the target):

  pip download argus-scanner semgrep -d wheels

Then either pass the directory to the package manager:

  sudo ARGUS_WHEELHOUSE=/media/wheels apt install ./argus-scanner_1.4.0-1_all.deb

or write the directory into the first line of /etc/argus-scanner/wheelhouse
and install normally.  The runtime can also be rebuilt afterwards:

  sudo argus-setup-runtime --wheelhouse /media/wheels

Set ARGUS_SKIP_RUNTIME_SETUP=1 to skip the download entirely.

Semgrep selection
-----------------
argus uses the Semgrep from its own runtime.  Set ARGUS_SEMGREP to force a
different binary:

  ARGUS_SEMGREP=/usr/local/bin/semgrep argus scan ...

pip honours the usual configuration (/etc/pip.conf, ~/.config/pip/pip.conf,
PIP_INDEX_URL), so an internal mirror can be used.

PEP 668
-------
Do not install Semgrep with the system interpreter:

  pip install semgrep          # fails: externally-managed-environment

Debian marks the system Python as externally managed.  The runtime
is a virtual environment, where pip skips that check, so
argus-setup-runtime is not affected.

GUI
---
The Tk front-end is in the same binary package.  It needs python3-tk
(Recommends) and a graphical session; the CLI works without either.

Offline dependency scanning
---------------------------
SCA uses api.osv.dev by default.  For offline use:

  argus db update
  argus sca . --offline

The database is stored in ~/.cache/argus/osv-db and can be copied between
machines.

